course: dictionary
lesson: 2538
title: Default: what happens when nobody decides otherwise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A default is the choice that is already set, and it is used unless someone changes it. Your tablet has a default font, so every word looks the same until you pick another one. Default can be a noun, a verb or an adjective, so the other words in the sentence tell you which job it is doing.
explain: The phrase «by default» means automatically, without anyone choosing. Look at the words around it. In «For a child today this means that God is not far away or angry by default», the words «this means» tell you the sentence is describing a starting picture. Swap in "automatically" and check: it still makes sense.
explain: Default has harder meanings too. To default on a loan means to fail to pay back money you owe. A team can win by default when the other team does not turn up. The context is the key: money, debts or a missing team tell you which meaning is used.
fact: Default means the setting or choice that is used unless you change it.
fact: «By default» means automatically, when nobody decides otherwise.
fact: Default can be a noun, a verb or an adjective, so check the sentence to see which one it is.
fact: «Default passwords» are the ones a device starts with, so change them to keep safe.
fact: «To default on a loan» means failing to pay back money you owe, and «win by default» means winning because the other side did not come or could not play.
exercise: «The phone uses the default font until you choose another.» What does default mean here? | A broken font | *The setting used unless you change it | The font you have to buy | The hardest font to read
exercise: «You won the match by default, because the other team did not turn up.» What does by default mean here? | In the rain | By your own skill and speed | *Because the other side did not come | After a long, hard fight
exercise: Dad says, «We will default on the loan if we cannot pay.» What does default on a loan mean? | Pay back the loan early | Ask the bank for a gift | Borrow even more money | *Fail to pay back money you owe
test: «Change the default password on your tablet to keep it safe.» Why should you change a default password? | *Because the starting one is easy for others to guess | Because it makes the tablet run faster | Because passwords must always be short | Because defaults are always the most secure choice
test: «By default, the game starts on level one.» What does by default mean here? | Without any sound at all | *Automatically, unless someone chooses otherwise | Only if someone asks for it | At the very end of the game
exam: What does default mean in «the default font» on a computer? | A broken screen | *The setting used unless someone changes it | A type of letter that is bold | A very fast game
